<div id=3D"page" lang=3D"en" dir=3D"ltr">
<div dir=3D"ltr" id=3D"content" lang=3D"en"><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"to=
p"></span>
<span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-1"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"li=
ne-2"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-3"></span><p class=3D"line86=
7">
</p><h2 id=3D"About">About</h2>
<span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-4"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"li=
ne-5"></span><p class=3D"line867"><a class=3D"https" href=3D"https://blogs.=
msdn.microsoft.com/commandline/2018/03/06/debian-gnulinux-for-wsl-now-avail=
able-in-the-windows-store/">As of March 2018</a> Debian is available for Wi=
ndows users through the Windows store as an app for the Windows Subsystem f=
or Linux (WSL). <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-6"></span><span class=3D"=
anchor" id=3D"line-7"></span></p><p class=3D"line862">The app gives you a D=
ebian stable command line environment running on the Windows kernel (WSL1) =
or Hyper-V with the new <a class=3D"https" href=3D"https://docs.microsoft.c=
om/en-us/windows/wsl/wsl2-install">WSL 2</a> interface depending on your Wi=
ndows 10 release version. <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-8"></span>Most =
of the packages in Debian stable should "just work". <span class=3D"anchor"=
 id=3D"line-9"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-10"></span></p><p c=
lass=3D"line867">
</p><h2 id=3D"Install">Install</h2>
<span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-11"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"l=
ine-12"></span><ul><li style=3D"list-style-type:none"><p class=3D"line891">=
<img alt=3D"&lt;!&gt;" height=3D"16" src=3D"https://wiki.debian.org/htdocs/=
debwiki/img/attention.png" title=3D"&lt;!&gt;" width=3D"16"> Note: As of th=
e time of writing, 2024-06-28, your best option for installing and using De=
bian GNU/Linux on WSL will probably be to use the WSL 2 subsystem and <tt c=
lass=3D"backtick">systemd</tt> mode. The Microsoft documentation for achiev=
ing this is rather fragmented. Therfore a detailed instruction is given in =
more detail under a separate heading <a href=3D"https://wiki.debian.org/Ins=
tallingDebianOn/Microsoft/Windows/SubsystemForLinux#WSL_2_with_systemd_supp=
ort">below</a>. <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-13"></span><span class=3D=
"anchor" id=3D"line-14"></span></p></li></ul><p class=3D"line862">To use th=
e store app you have to enable the WSL subsystem first by following the <a =
class=3D"https" href=3D"https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/instal=
l-win10">guide</a>. <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-15"></span><span clas=
s=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-16"></span></p><p class=3D"line862">Afterwards just=
 install the <a class=3D"https" href=3D"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/p/d=
ebian/9msvkqc78pk6">Debian</a> app from the Microsoft Store. <span class=3D=
"anchor" id=3D"line-17"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-18"></span=
></p><p class=3D"line874">You will be asked to define a user and password u=
pon first start. This user will also be given sudo rights. <span class=3D"a=
nchor" id=3D"line-19"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-20"></span><=
/p><p class=3D"line862">There is a way to <a class=3D"https" href=3D"https:=
//docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/install-on-server">install the Debia=
n WSL distro offline</a> &amp; without using Microsoft Market. <span class=
=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-21"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-22"></s=
pan></p><p class=3D"line862">Further information about the ongoing developm=
ent of WSL can be found in the <a class=3D"https" href=3D"https://blogs.msd=
n.microsoft.com/commandline/tag/wsl/">WSL tag</a> of the Microsoft blog. <s=
pan class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-23"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"lin=
e-24"></span></p><p class=3D"line867">
</p><h2 id=3D"WSL_2_with_systemd_support">WSL 2 with systemd support</h2>
<span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-25"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"l=
ine-26"></span><p class=3D"line862">Microsoft partnered with Canonical to <=
a class=3D"https" href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/sys=
temd#systemd-demo-video">bring systemd support to WSL 2</a>, and it is also=
 available for Debian and other GNU/Linux distributions. <span class=3D"anc=
hor" id=3D"line-27"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-28"></span></p=
><p class=3D"line862">WSL 2 with <tt class=3D"backtick">systemd</tt> is pro=
bably what you want for your freshly installed Debian GNU/Linux system, as =
WSL 2 is a prerequisite for <a href=3D"https://wiki.debian.org/InstallingDe=
bianOn/Microsoft/Windows/SubsystemForLinux#Advanced_Usage">GUI application =
support</a>, and <tt class=3D"backtick">systemd</tt> is a prerequisite for =
many Debian packages. Read more about GUI apps <a class=3D"https" href=3D"h=
ttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/tutorials/gui-apps">here</a>. =
<span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-29"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"l=
ine-30"></span></p><p class=3D"line862">At the time of this writing, 2024-0=
6-28, the documentation over at <a class=3D"https" href=3D"https://learn.mi=
crosoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/install-manual">Microsoft Learn</a> for aciev=
ing a Debian install in a WSL 2 subsystem with <tt class=3D"backtick">syste=
md</tt> activated is rather fragmented. Therefore the process is detailed h=
ere. <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-31"></span></p><ul><li style=3D"list=
-style-type:none"><p class=3D"line891"><img alt=3D"&lt;!&gt;" height=3D"16"=
 src=3D"https://wiki.debian.org/htdocs/debwiki/img/attention.png" title=3D"=
&lt;!&gt;" width=3D"16"> Note that a Windows 11 operating system for hostin=
g WSL is assumed. <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-32"></span><span class=
=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-33"></span></p></li></ul><p class=3D"line874">Lengtl=
y description follows here: <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-34"></span><s=
pan class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-35"></span></p><p class=3D"line867">
</p><h3 id=3D"To_prepare_your_system:">To prepare your system:</h3>
<span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-36"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"l=
ine-37"></span><ol type=3D"1"><li>Make sure your computer has the Virtualiz=
ation features enabled in UEFI Settings (some may refer to this as BIOS Set=
tings). <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-38"></span></li><li><p class=3D"l=
ine862">Activate and install the needed features and software on your Windo=
ws host OS. Open PowerShell in Administrator mode and type these commands: =
<span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-39"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"l=
ine-40"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-41"></span><span class=3D"=
anchor" id=3D"line-42"></span></p><pre><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-1"=
></span> dism.exe /online /enable-feature /featurename:Microsoft-Windows-Su=
bsystem-Linux /all /norestart
<span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-2"></span> dism.exe /online /enable-featu=
re /featurename:VirtualMachinePlatform /all /norestart</pre><span class=3D"=
anchor" id=3D"line-43"></span></li><li>Reboot your Windows 11 host <span cl=
ass=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-44"></span></li><li><p class=3D"line862">Update y=
our WSL Linux kernel update package. Open <tt class=3D"backtick">PowerShell=
</tt> in administrator mode and enter the ffollowing command <span class=3D=
"anchor" id=3D"line-45"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-46"></span=
><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-47"></span></p><pre><span class=3D"ancho=
r" id=3D"line-1-1"></span> wsl.exe --update</pre><span class=3D"anchor" id=
=3D"line-48"></span><ul><li>This will install and update WSL from Microsoft=
 Store <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-49"></span></li><li><p class=3D"li=
ne862">If you do dot wish or cannot use Microsoft Store, please consult thi=
s <a class=3D"https" href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/=
install-manual">Microsoft Learn article</a> <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"li=
ne-50"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-51"></span></p></li></ul></=
li></ol><p class=3D"line867">
</p><h3 id=3D"To_install_Debian_GNU.2FLinux">To install Debian GNU/Linux</h=
3>
<span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-52"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"l=
ine-53"></span><ol type=3D"1"><li><p class=3D"line862">Giong forward we are=
 in usermode. So you must open normal <tt class=3D"backtick">PowerShell</tt=
> without administrator mode for the steps in this section. <span class=3D"=
anchor" id=3D"line-54"></span></p></li><li>Set WSL 2 as you default WSL ver=
sion. This is a per-user setting in Windows.   <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D=
"line-55"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-56"></span><span class=
=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-57"></span><pre><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-1-=
2"></span> wsl --set-default-version 2</pre><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"li=
ne-58"></span></li><li>Install Debian <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-59"=
></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-60"></span><span class=3D"anchor"=
 id=3D"line-61"></span><pre><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-1-3"></span> =
wsl --install -d Debian</pre><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-62"></span><=
ul><li>This takes some time <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-63"></span></=
li></ul></li><li><p class=3D"line862">Set a <tt class=3D"backtick">username=
</tt> and <tt class=3D"backtick">password</tt> for your Debian GNU/Linux in=
stallation when prompted <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-64"></span></p><=
ul><li>You are now logged in to your Debian system in command line mode <sp=
an class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-65"></span></li></ul></li><li><p class=3D"li=
ne862">Add some text to the file <tt class=3D"backtick">/etc/wsl.conf</tt> =
to activate <tt class=3D"backtick">systemd</tt> mode on next boot of WSL 2 =
<span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-66"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"l=
ine-67"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-68"></span><span class=3D"=
anchor" id=3D"line-69"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-70"></span>=
</p><pre><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-1-4"></span> sudo echo '
<span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-2-1"></span> [boot]
<span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-3"></span> systemd=3Dtrue' &gt;&gt; /etc/=
wsl.conf</pre><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-71"></span>Provide the user=
 password you set in the previous step when prompted.  <span class=3D"ancho=
r" id=3D"line-72"></span></li><li><p class=3D"line862">Verify the content o=
f the file <tt class=3D"backtick">/etc/wsl.conf</tt> and correct any errror=
s. There should be only one section [boot] and exactly one instance of the =
line <tt class=3D"backtick">systemd=3Dtrue</tt> in it. <span class=3D"ancho=
r" id=3D"line-73"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-74"></span><span=
 class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-75"></span></p><pre><span class=3D"anchor" id=
=3D"line-1-5"></span> sudo editor /etc/wsl.conf</pre><span class=3D"anchor"=
 id=3D"line-76"></span></li><li><p class=3D"line862">Exit to PowerShell by =
issuing the command <tt class=3D"backtick">logout</tt>, or by pressing <tt =
class=3D"backtick">[Ctrl]&nbsp;+&nbsp;D</tt> <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"l=
ine-77"></span></p></li><li><p class=3D"line862">Shut down your Debian WSL =
2 instance from PowerShell <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-78"></span><sp=
an class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-79"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line=
-80"></span></p><pre><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-1-6"></span> wsl --s=
hutdown -d Debian</pre><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-81"></span></li><l=
i>Start your Debian instance and log back in <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"l=
ine-82"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-83"></span><span class=3D"=
anchor" id=3D"line-84"></span><pre><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-1-7"><=
/span> wsl -d Debian -u &lt;username&gt;</pre><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"=
line-85"></span></li><li><p class=3D"line862">Use <tt class=3D"backtick">ap=
t</tt> to upgrade your WSL 2 Debian and <tt class=3D"backtick">apt</tt> or =
<tt class=3D"backtick">aptitude</tt> to install some packages (<tt class=3D=
"backtick">mesa-utils</tt> is required on the Debian side for the GUI apps =
integration to work) <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-86"></span><span cla=
ss=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-87"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-88"><=
/span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-89"></span><span class=3D"anchor" i=
d=3D"line-90"></span></p><pre><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-1-8"></span=
> sudo apt update
<span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-2-2"></span> sudo apt dist-upgrade
<span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-3-1"></span> sudo apt install mesa-utils =
firefox-esr</pre><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-91"></span></li><li>The =
installed programs can be started from a Debian shell, or from the Windows =
start menu. <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-92"></span><span class=3D"anc=
hor" id=3D"line-93"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-94"></span></l=
i></ol><p class=3D"line867">
</p><h2 id=3D"Advanced_Usage">Advanced Usage</h2>
<span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-95"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"l=
ine-96"></span><p class=3D"line862">WSL 2 brings GUI application and <tt cl=
ass=3D"backtick">sytemd</tt> support to WSL. That is, you now can run Debia=
n apps in an integrated desktop mode. <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-97"=
></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-98"></span></p><p class=3D"line86=
2">To activate the new <a class=3D"https" href=3D"https://docs.microsoft.co=
m/en-us/windows/wsl/tutorials/gui-apps">GUI application support</a> you hav=
e to update your WSL 2 environment to <a href=3D"https://wiki.debian.org/De=
bianBookworm">Debian bookworm</a> or later. <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"li=
ne-99"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-100"></span></p><p class=3D=
"line862">After that you need to install <tt class=3D"backtick">mesa-utils<=
/tt> this will install all the necessary packages for th GUI app support to=
 work. <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-101"></span><span class=3D"anchor"=
 id=3D"line-102"></span></p><p class=3D"line874">Most of the GUI apps in De=
bian should now just work out-of-the-box (e.g., try firefox). <span class=
=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-103"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-104"><=
/span></p><p class=3D"line867">
</p><h2 id=3D"Feedback">Feedback</h2>
<span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-105"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"=
line-106"></span><p class=3D"line874">Please use the Microsoft Store review=
/feedback to report bugs or feature requests for now. <span class=3D"anchor=
" id=3D"line-107"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-108"></span></p>=
<p class=3D"line874">There is a IRC channel on OFTC to discuss WSL related =
stuff: #debian-wsl <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-109"></span><span clas=
s=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-110"></span></p><p class=3D"line862">You can also l=
eave patches and issues at the <a class=3D"https" href=3D"https://salsa.deb=
ian.org/Debian/WSL">WSL repo on Salsa</a>. <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"lin=
e-111"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-112"></span></p><p class=3D=
"line867">
</p><h2 id=3D"Known_Issues">Known Issues</h2>
<span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-113"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"=
line-114"></span><p class=3D"line874">Any software relying on systemd or lo=
w-level hardware accessibility might fail due to missing support from the c=
urrent Windows kernel or virtualization interface. <span class=3D"anchor" i=
d=3D"line-115"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-116"></span></p><p =
class=3D"line867"><tt class=3D"backtick">systemd</tt> support has been adde=
d to WSL 2. See description of this <a href=3D"https://wiki.debian.org/Inst=
allingDebianOn/Microsoft/Windows/SubsystemForLinux#WSL_2_with_systemd_suppo=
rt">above</a>. <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-117"></span><span class=3D=
"anchor" id=3D"line-118"></span></p><p class=3D"line874">As WSL is a pretty=
 new project from Microsoft improvement can be expected to happen with ever=
y new Windows stable channel release (approx. every 6 months). <span class=
=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-119"></span>The app launcher will be updated to supp=
ort stable release features continuously. <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line=
-120"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-121"></span></p><p class=3D"=
line862">If WSL itself is installed from Microsoft Store, for example by is=
suing <tt class=3D"backtick">wsl&nbsp;--update</tt> in an elevated PowerShe=
ll prompt on the Windows Host, Microsoft claims WSL will be updated more fr=
equently and independently of the Windows stable chanel releases. <span cla=
ss=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-122"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-123"=
></span></p><p class=3D"line867">
</p><h3 id=3D"FAQ">FAQ</h3>
<span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-124"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"=
line-125"></span><dl><dt>How do I keep my Debian environment up-to-date </d=
t><dd><p class=3D"line862">as with any other Debian installation use apt/ap=
t-get to install and update software from the official Debian mirrors (e.g.=
, <tt class=3D"backtick">apt&nbsp;update&nbsp;&amp;&amp;&nbsp;apt&nbsp;dist=
-upgrade</tt>) <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-126"></span><span class=3D=
"anchor" id=3D"line-127"></span></p></dd><dt>How do I install a newer relea=
se? </dt><dd>You can install the app, change your sources.list and upgrade =
your install as with every other Debian installation. <span class=3D"anchor=
" id=3D"line-128"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-129"></span></dd=
><dt>How many people are using Debian via WSL? </dt><dd>Approximately 1,746=
,662 at last count (unique installs according to the Microsoft Partner Cent=
er dashboard 2024-11-20). <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-130"></span><sp=
an class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-131"></span></dd></dl><p class=3D"line867">
</p><h2 id=3D"Code_.26_Issues">Code &amp; Issues</h2>
<span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-132"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"=
line-133"></span><p class=3D"line862">The full app code and all build depen=
dencies can be found in the <a class=3D"https" href=3D"https://salsa.debian=
.org/Debian/WSL">WSL repo on salsa</a>. <span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"line-1=
34"></span><span class=3D"anchor" id=3D"bottom"></span></p></div><div id=3D=
"pagebottom"></div>
</div>


